{:type :constraint
 :id :constraint/propagator-merge-laws
 :text "Cell merge must be commutative, idempotent and associative on valid domain contents under the domain-defined semantic equality. Normalize permissive external representations at the boundary; do not use representation differences to excuse order-dependent meaning. Strongest projection is a separate operation and must not replace raw content to manufacture these laws."
 :created-at #inst "2026-10-18T09:34:18.000Z"
 :scope "Partial-information policy"
 :source "user-instruction:2026-10-18"
 :status :active :lifecycle :candidate :evidence-state :needs-verification
 :applies-to [:component/propagator-information :component/propagator-kernel]
 :supported-by [:evidence/propagator-information]
 :verification "Check merge(a,b)=merge(b,a), merge(a,a)=a, and merge(merge(a,b),c)=merge(a,merge(b,c)) across normalized domain values, duplicates, conflicts, partial values and support/retraction cases. State semantic equality and normalization explicitly; finite tests do not prove every domain."}

{:type :constraint
 :id :constraint/propagator-flat-gur-canonical
 :text "Flat GUR is the canonical GUR for new recursive declaration and compiler composition. Accumulating and other GUR implementations are explicit alternatives or historical baselines and must not compete as the default semantic authority."
 :created-at #inst "2026-10-18T09:34:18.000Z"
 :scope "Recursive declaration / compiler composition"
 :source "user-instruction:2026-10-18"
 :status :active :lifecycle :candidate :evidence-state :needs-verification
